With --provider openai, the four GPT-6 ids (gpt-6-sol, which is the default, gpt-6-luna, gpt-6-astra, gpt-6.1-sol) now go to OpenAI's Responses endpoint (/v1/responses) instead of /v1/chat/completions. Tool-using runs on the default openai model were going to the endpoint OpenAI says doesn't support function calling for these models. I only checked this against a local stub server. There's no key here, so no real OpenAI call was made. Committed as 34263eed.

What changed
• The plan's one-line fix wasn't enough. yoyo hardcoded the Chat Completions provider in all three OpenAI-family agent builders (main, /side, architect), so changing the model config alone left the wire exactly as before. I added a small helper, openai_family_agent: a Responses config now gets yoagent's Responses provider, and everything else keeps today's path.
• Sub-agents: the sub-agent builder in src/tools.rs makes the same choice.
• Other openai ids (gpt-4o, gpt-5, …) are unchanged and still use Chat Completions.
• The old comment claiming this "cannot be verified without a key" is gone from the code. It's recorded as a superseded claim in ARCHITECTURE.md, with a CHANGELOG line under Unreleased.

Tests
• The new tests/openai_responses_wire.rs runs the real binary against a stub that records each request. It strips inherited API keys and passes a dummy one, so it should pass in CI, which exports no keys. It checks three things:
  • gpt-6-sol goes to /v1/responses with 12 tools in the body;
  • gpt-4o still goes to /v1/chat/completions;
  • with --thinking high the body carries effort high and no temperature.
• The old …_keeps_the_wire test is renamed and now asserts the Responses wire. The non-GPT-6 test now checks that the endpoint type, URL and compatibility settings are unchanged.
• I broke each half of the fix on purpose, one at a time, and restored it each time. Each break turned both gpt-6-sol tests red by name while gpt-4o stayed green.
• build, the full test suite, clippy, fmt, the module-size gate and harness_logic.sh all pass. agent_builder.rs grew by 13 lines, inside its 20-line allowance.

Still open, filed as #1060
• If you use --provider openai with a GPT-6 id against a third-party --base-url, requests now go to /responses. A server that only has /chat/completions will return 404, and there's no setting to switch back yet.
• Passing --temperature explicitly still sends it alongside the reasoning effort, and OpenAI probably rejects that with a 400 on every call. I captured the request bodies as evidence. It's not a one-line fix, so I left it out.
• Other openai reasoning ids (gpt-5.x, the o-series) still use Chat Completions.
• Nothing tests which endpoint sub-agents actually call.

The docs census found no user-facing sentence about the openai endpoint, so models.md is untouched.
